WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.620
Supergirl is about to make history.

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:08.400
During a San Diego Comic-Con panel on July
21st, 2018, the CW announced that Nicole Maines

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:14.380
will join Supergirl in Season 4 as Nia Nal,
aka Dreamer, the first transgender superhero

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:15.380
on television.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:20.180
"It feels fitting to say that with great power
comes great responsibility."

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.490
Described by Deadline as "a soulful young
transgender woman with a fierce drive to protect

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:28.360
others," Nia reportedly won't start out as
a full-fledged vigilante.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:33.610
Instead, the upcoming storyline will see Nia,
a new member of CatCo's reporting team, gradually

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:36.570
"fulfilling her destiny" to become the superhero
Dreamer.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:40.300
"Nia is so much more than 'The Trans Superhero.'

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.910
She is a reporter, she is hopeful, she is
good."

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.940
Deadline speculates that the character's evolution
from Nia into Dreamer will be similar to the

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:52.780
way Melissa Benoist's Kara grew and matured
to become Supergirl as she stands today.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:57.761
The character is a new iteration of DC Comics'
Nura Nal, aka Dream Girl, who made her comics

00:00:57.761 --> 00:01:02.970
debut in 1964 and was given the codename "Dreamer"
in one '90s storyline.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:06.409
Nicole Maines made national headlines when
she was just a young teen.

00:01:06.409 --> 00:01:09.890
After the grandfather of a classmate at Maines'
elementary school in Orono, Maine complained

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:13.619
to school officials that Maines shouldn't
be allowed to use the girls' restroom - and

00:01:13.619 --> 00:01:17.189
the school agreed - the Maines family sued
her school district.

00:01:17.189 --> 00:01:21.729
In June of 2014, the Maine Supreme Judicial
Court found that the school district was in

00:01:21.729 --> 00:01:26.240
violation of the Human Rights Act, and ruled
that trans students should be allowed to use

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.330
the restroom assigned to the gender with which
they identify.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:33.850
Since then, Maines has been an outspoken activist
for the LGBTQ community.

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:38.429
In 2015, Maines and her family were the subject
of Washington Post writer Amy Ellis Nutt's

00:01:38.429 --> 00:01:43.219
book Becoming Nicole: The Extraordinary Transformation
of an Ordinary Family, which chronicles the

00:01:43.219 --> 00:01:47.189
Maines family's journey to better understand
and celebrate their daughter's identity.

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:51.659
That same year, Maines made her television
debut in an episode of USA Network's Royal

00:01:51.659 --> 00:01:57.069
Pains, portraying a trans teen and choreographer
named Anna whose hormones posed a potential

00:01:57.069 --> 00:01:58.459
risk to her heath.

00:01:58.459 --> 00:02:03.599
In 2016, Maines was featured in HBO's The
Trans List, a documentary directed by Timothy

00:02:03.599 --> 00:02:08.959
Greenfield-Sanders that highlights the stories
of 11 transgender individuals including Caitlyn

00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:12.569
Jenner and Orange Is the New Black actress
Laverne Cox.

00:02:12.569 --> 00:02:16.940
More recently, Maines spoke out about Scarlett
Johansson's involvement in the film Rub and

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:17.940
Tug.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:22.239
Johansson was set to portray transgender gangster
and massage parlor owner Dante "Tex" Gill,

00:02:22.239 --> 00:02:25.510
but dropped out of the project due to subsequent
backlash.

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:26.519
Maines told Variety,

00:02:26.519 --> 00:02:30.840
"With trans folks, we have a lot of people
accusing us of just playing dress up for whatever

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.230
reason, and that's not true.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:36.650
And so having trans people play trans roles
shows that we are valid in our identity and

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:38.340
we deserve to exist as we do."

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:42.519
It's for this reason that Maines' involvement
in Supergirl is not just exciting but also

00:02:42.519 --> 00:02:44.040
incredibly important.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.129
And Maines isn't the only new addition to
Supergirl's fourth season.

00:02:47.129 --> 00:02:51.860
April Parker Jones is set to play Colonel
Haley, described by Deadline as a "hardline

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:56.290
career military woman" fiercely dedicated
to her country and loyal to a fault to her

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:57.400
commanding officers.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:02.829
David Ajala is also on board as the devilishly
charming and witty antihero Manchester Black.

00:03:02.829 --> 00:03:07.900
Supergirl introducing Maines' Nia Nal as TV's
first transgender superhero sets an incredible

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:13.250
precedent and opens the doors for even more
positive LGBTQ representation on the small

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.250
screen.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:18.359
Will we see Alysia Yeoh, Batgirl's best friend,
roommate, and a transgender woman - in a DC

00:03:18.359 --> 00:03:19.860
series in the future?

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:24.519
The Batgirl comic even featured Yeoh getting
married in 2015, marking the first transgender

00:03:24.519 --> 00:03:26.510
wedding in mainstream comic book history.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:30.719
For now, we can look forward to seeing Maines
team up with the rest of the Supergirl crew

00:03:30.719 --> 00:03:33.760
when Season 4 premieres October 14th on the
CW.

